7189	{"artifactId":"LLD-401ae5fb7b8537cc-s4","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-401ae5fb7b8537cc-s4-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:controller","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-09-22T14:04:56.990Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"cl1","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared sc1 IPC client exists as SharedIpcClient with an rpc method and a status method, the sole daemon path the gateway uses.","evidence":"CONFIRMED: sc1 SharedIpcClient lives at src/shared/ipc-client.ts (owner Story ad0d45c9:S001) and is already consumed inside vscode-plugin (config/gateway.ts, workspace/registrar.ts uses client.rpc). The rpc/status surface is real.","action":"No change — the gateway correctly leans on the existing sc1 client.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl2","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"A daemon.status IPC method exists and returns a DaemonStatus with uptime/repos/queueDepth/embeddingsPending (mapped to DaemonStatusView).","evidence":"CONFIRMED: daemon.status is a real IPC method (src/cli/services/daemon.ts: rpc<DaemonStatus>('daemon.status'); daemon handler + server-registry test exercise it). DaemonStatus type with queueDepth/embeddingsPending exists.","action":"No change — status() maps a real payload.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl3","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"A repo.list IPC method exists (mapped to registeredRepos()).","evidence":"CONFIRMED: repo.list handler exists at src/daemon/index.ts:536 and is already called from vscode-plugin/src/workspace/registrar.ts:40 (client.rpc('repo.list')).","action":"No change — registeredRepos() maps a real IPC.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl4","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"A daemon.debug-status IPC method exists and returns { clients: AttachedClient[] } (mapped to mcpClients()).","evidence":"PARTIALLY PRECISE: daemon.debug-status + AttachedClient are real (src/shared/types.ts, src/cli/services/debug-types.ts). But the actual payload is a UNION { reachable:true; clients: readonly AttachedClient[] } | { reachable:false; ... }, not a bare { clients: AttachedClient[] } as the LLD abbreviates. mcpClients() must read clients only on the reachable branch.","action":"Build-time note (not a design defect): when wiring mcpClients(), destructure the debug-status union's reachable branch before mapping clients; treat unreachable as an empty McpClientView[] or a GatewayReadError. Carry this into the s6 consumer too.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The LLD's { clients } shorthand is accurate for the reachable case but omits the reachable discriminator the real IPC returns; the plan/build step should map only the reachable branch's clients."}},{"claimId":"cl5","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The sc2 status-bar surface is StatusSurface over an injected StatusBarHandle (surfaces/types.ts) that has text/tooltip/show but NO `command` field, so the click command is set on the raw vscode StatusBarItem in extension.ts.","evidence":"CONFIRMED: surfaces/types.ts:17 `export interface StatusBarHandle extends DisposableLike` has no `command` field; extension.ts:52-54 creates the raw vscode StatusBarItem and casts it to StatusBarHandle. So the click command must be set on the raw StatusBarItem in extension.ts, exactly as the LLD states.","action":"No change — the ac1 wiring approach is sound.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl6","kind":"closed-union","severity":"LOW","premise":"InsrcCommandId is a closed union in surfaces/command-registry.ts and was additively extended by S003 for 'insrc.settings.refresh' (the precedent this story follows); the three new ids are additive.","evidence":"CONFIRMED: command-registry.ts:22 shows the InsrcCommandId closed union ending with 'insrc.settings.refresh' (the S003 additive precedent). No insrc.status.* ids exist yet in vscode-plugin/src, so the three new ids are genuinely additive.","action":"No change — additive-union extension matches the established pattern.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl7","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"extension.ts is the SOLE module importing 'vscode' (the injectable-seam convention the sc9 cores preserve).","evidence":"CONFIRMED: the only `import * as vscode from 'vscode'` inside vscode-plugin/src is extension.ts:12 (other matches are tests/docs). The sole-vscode-importer invariant holds.","action":"No change — the sc9 cores must stay VS-Code-free over injected boundaries.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl8","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The compile-only src/vscode.d.ts shim currently declares StatusBarItem.command but NOT the Webview (createWebviewPanel/WebviewPanel/ViewColumn) or QuickPick (showQuickPick/QuickPickItem) API — these are net-new additive declarations.","evidence":"CONFIRMED: vscode.d.ts declares StatusBarItem (line 13, with command) but has NO createWebviewPanel/WebviewPanel/showQuickPick/QuickPickItem anywhere in vscode-plugin/src (all 44 such matches are in docs). These are net-new additive shim declarations, as the LLD says.","action":"No change — additive shim extension is required and correctly scoped.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl9","kind":"inventory","severity":"LOW","premise":"The panels module (src/panels/) is net-new — no existing panels/webview-host/daemon-gateway files.","evidence":"CONFIRMED: no createWebviewPanelHost/createDaemonDataGateway/DaemonDataGateway symbols exist in vscode-plugin/src (all 37 matches are docs). src/panels/ is genuinely net-new.","action":"No change — new-capability module, no collision.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl10","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The test convention is node:test over injected fakes with existing suites surfaces.test.ts / controller.test.ts / sync-engine.test.ts, and command-count tests in packaging.test.ts + workspace/__tests__/activation.test.ts.","evidence":"CONFIRMED: node:test is the pervasive convention (40 test hits); surfaces.test.ts / controller.test.ts / sync-engine.test.ts all exist. The packaging + activation command-count tests are the ones S003 already had to touch.","action":"No change — test strategy matches the shipped convention.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl11","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"sc9 is owned by this story (s4) per the HLD boundary, and the LLD implements it verbatim from the HLD interfaceSketch (DetailTab triad, WebviewPanelHost 2 methods, DaemonDataGateway 5 methods) with no added surface members.","evidence":"CONFIRMED: the HLD boundary assigns sc9 ownership to s4, and the LLD implements the interfaceSketch verbatim (DetailTab triad, 2 host methods, 5 gateway methods, view types) with showStatusMenu flagged as an internal (non-surface) host method — no added sc9 members.","action":"No change — the implements-verbatim trace holds.","fixability":"manual"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":11},"reviewedAt":"2026-09-22T14:04:56.990Z","model":"client"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
